==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|res|rēs|lang=la|thing, matter, affair}} {{term|iudicata|iūdicata|lang=la}}, past participle of {{term|iudico|iūdico|lang=la|judge}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[res]] [[judicata]]|res judicatae}}

# {{legal}} An issue that is before a court, has already been decided by another court, and that therefore must be dismissed by the current court.

